 Banking Operations: Unsupervised Email Requirement Discovery


​ Project Overview & Business Strategy


​In high-volume banking operations, client queues are continuously saturated with unstructured email communications. Processing these items manually or forcing them into rigid, pre-defined classification categories restricts operational visibility, creating massive blind spots for emerging transactional patterns or structural operational shifts.
​This platform delivers an end-to-end MLOps pipeline orchestrated within Microsoft Fabric to ingest, clean, transform, and map raw email files. Crucially, this is an unsupervised discovery system, not a traditional classifier:
​No Predefined Labels: The algorithm surfaces themes natively without human data-annotation costs.
​No Fixed Output Schemas: The data defines the categories dynamically.
​Proportional Theme Generation: The engine proposes candidate clusters while a Human-in-the-Loop audit isolates real operational requirements from systemic data artifacts.



Core Infrastructure & Medallion Design


​The broader data platform relies on a decoupled Medallion Architecture to guarantee data lineage, clean transformation paths, and reliable downstream machine learning servings.

Architectural Logic Flow

​The  internal mechanics of the discovery engine are split into four clear macro-stages, ranging from infrastructure provisioning to final distributed lakehouse persistence.
Step-by-Step Technical Execution
​Stage 0: Environment Initialization & Configuration

